WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:05.011
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.011 --> 00:08.493
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.493 --> 00:11.873
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.873 --> 00:15.084
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:15.084 --> 00:18.537
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.537 --> 00:21.847
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.847 --> 00:23.422
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.422 --> 00:24.796
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.796 --> 00:32.963
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.975 --> 00:37.348
TV ANNOUNCER:
The Travel Channel presents,

00:37.348 --> 00:39.727
"Backpacking Through Europe
with a Bowlegged Man

00:39.727 --> 00:41.232
in Short Shorts."

00:41.232 --> 00:44.714
Hello. Come, let's see some
beautiful sites together.

00:44.714 --> 00:47.233
Hello, Tree.
Thank you for shade.

00:47.233 --> 00:48.698
Hello, Mountain Cat.

00:48.698 --> 00:51.416
Thank you for controlling
local rat population.

00:51.416 --> 00:52.750
Hello, Windmill.

00:52.750 --> 00:55.460
Thank you for the cheese ride
and ball cooling.

00:55.460 --> 00:57.607
Next week, bullet trains.

00:57.607 --> 01:00.256
Hello...!

01:00.256 --> 01:02.394
Hey, Dad. Are you busy?

01:02.394 --> 01:05.272
I was thinking we could
spend some time together.

01:05.272 --> 01:06.949
Okay, are you a
television set,

01:06.949 --> 01:07.981
or the Internet?

01:07.981 --> 01:08.925
No.

01:08.925 --> 01:10.359
Oh, then no.
No, thank you.

01:10.359 --> 01:11.634
Are you sure?

01:11.634 --> 01:13.441
Cause there's a
three-day weekend coming up

01:13.441 --> 01:15.789
and I thought maybe you and I
can finally go fishing

01:15.789 --> 01:17.293
like we've been
talking about.

01:17.293 --> 01:20.645
Aw, sorry, Chris, I can't.
I got insanity practice.

01:20.645 --> 01:21.909
(yelling hysterically)

01:21.909 --> 01:24.357
Pinwheels! Pinwheels in my head!

01:24.357 --> 01:26.063
Voices! Angry fish!

01:26.063 --> 01:27.769
How's he doing?
Not good.

01:27.769 --> 01:30.487
He still thinks this is
"practice" of some sort.

01:30.487 --> 01:33.468
But you promised
we'd go fishing.

01:33.468 --> 01:36.649
Aw, Chris, I was just
lying to you so you'd go away.

01:36.649 --> 01:39.860
But, if you leave me alone now,
I'll give you a billion dollars.

01:39.860 --> 01:41.966
You've got a deal!

01:41.966 --> 01:43.412
Peter, you know,
i-it might help Chris

01:43.412 --> 01:45.247
to be able to spend
some time with his father.

01:45.247 --> 01:46.822
Well, what's in it
for ol' Pete?

01:46.822 --> 01:47.996
He's your son.

01:47.996 --> 01:49.602
Don't you want someone
to bond with.

01:49.602 --> 01:52.382
No. I only form
unspoken bonds.

01:52.382 --> 01:56.867
(tires screech)

01:56.867 --> 02:00.518
PAT BENATAR (on radio):
♪ Hit me with your best shot

02:00.518 --> 02:02.255
♪ Why don't you hit me
with your best shot? ♪

02:02.255 --> 02:03.600
(increases volume)

02:03.600 --> 02:04.804
♪

02:04.804 --> 02:06.669
♪ Hit me with your best shot

02:06.669 --> 02:07.943
(increases volume)

02:07.943 --> 02:10.522
♪ Fire away...

02:10.522 --> 02:12.729
(increases volume)

02:12.729 --> 02:17.787
♪ You come on
with a "come on"... ♪

02:17.787 --> 02:19.162
O-Okay.

02:19.162 --> 02:21.138
I'll talk to you later. Bye.

02:21.138 --> 02:22.372
You guys, that was my mom.

02:22.372 --> 02:24.189
She said that
Daddy broke his leg.

02:24.189 --> 02:25.291
How?!

02:25.291 --> 02:27.901
A-Apparently, he got hurt
at the mall.

02:27.901 --> 02:30.378
Carter, please stop
doing that.

02:30.378 --> 02:32.316
We need to get you
some new corduroys.

02:32.316 --> 02:34.864
No! None of the other boys
are wearing corduroys!

02:34.864 --> 02:36.199
I want dungarees!

02:36.199 --> 02:38.076
You're going to
get hurt doing that.

02:38.076 --> 02:41.056
No I'm not!
I'm the champ at doing this!

02:41.056 --> 02:42.962
Ow! You jinxed me!

02:42.962 --> 02:44.005
Aw, damn it!

02:44.005 --> 02:45.339
Hey, call that beeping cart

02:45.339 --> 02:47.558
that carries around
the fat black people.

02:47.558 --> 02:49.864
Well, I guess Babs has
her work cut out for her.

02:49.864 --> 02:52.744
Actually, Mom can't take care
of him, she's out of town

02:52.744 --> 02:58.664
doing a photo shoot for the
cover of Veins Magazine.

02:58.664 --> 03:00.882
So, are you gonna go
take care of him, Mom?

03:00.882 --> 03:03.923
I can't go. I've got to go get
my hair very minutely changed

03:03.923 --> 03:09.611
and then spend the next 14 hours
trying to get people to notice.

03:09.611 --> 03:10.786
Well...?

03:10.786 --> 03:12.691
Lois, move.
You're blocking the TV.

03:12.691 --> 03:14.838
(laughs)
What do you think?

03:14.838 --> 03:16.474
I think you're
blocking the TV.

03:16.474 --> 03:19.223
Peter, i-is there anything
you want to say to me?

03:19.223 --> 03:20.427
(sighs)

03:20.427 --> 03:22.574
All right.
Amy at work kissed me.

03:22.574 --> 03:24.753
It is true
that I did not step away,

03:24.753 --> 03:26.057
but I did not lean in.

03:26.057 --> 03:27.561
However, in my defense,

03:27.561 --> 03:30.040
she had recently gotten
her hair done differently.

03:30.040 --> 03:32.950
I was actually thinking that
maybe you could go help Daddy.

03:32.950 --> 03:34.324
Well, not me, Mom.

03:34.324 --> 03:35.729
Last time I was
at Grandpa's,

03:35.729 --> 03:38.278
I beat him at checkers and he
punched one of my hogans.

03:38.278 --> 03:39.411
Well, what about Chris?

03:39.411 --> 03:41.288
Wai-Wait, where is Chris?

03:41.288 --> 03:42.662
He's upstairs
in his room.

03:42.662 --> 03:44.468
That's odd.
He never misses a meal.

03:44.468 --> 03:46.005
I-I better go check on him.

03:46.005 --> 03:47.218
Yeah, good idea.

03:47.218 --> 03:51.964
I better check on my
hairless twin in the storm shed.

03:51.964 --> 03:54.613
Close the door,
the moonlight burns!

03:54.613 --> 03:57.020
It's almost Christmas.
It's almost Christmas.

03:57.020 --> 03:58.366
Christmas?!

03:58.366 --> 03:59.769
Yes. Keep being good

03:59.769 --> 04:02.780
and all the eggshells and
coffee grounds will be yours.

04:02.780 --> 04:04.625
Can I meet the family?

04:04.625 --> 04:06.633
You've overstepped!
No Christmas!

04:06.633 --> 04:10.244
(door slams shut)

04:10.244 --> 04:12.251
Hey, Chris. Are you okay?

04:12.251 --> 04:14.701
Holy crap, it smells
like farts in here.

04:14.701 --> 04:16.436
Those are my farts.

04:16.436 --> 04:19.115
Why doesn't Dad ever
want to spend time with me?

04:19.115 --> 04:21.623
Chris, come here.

04:21.629 --> 04:22.697
Sit down.

04:22.697 --> 04:24.744
You know I love you,
right, sweetie?

04:24.744 --> 04:27.183
Mom... not in front
of my posters.

04:27.183 --> 04:29.159
And your father
loves you, too.

04:29.159 --> 04:32.038
He just has trouble
expressing his emotions.

04:32.038 --> 04:33.985
PETER:
I love Mike & Molly!

04:33.985 --> 04:36.564
I love Mike
and I also love Molly!

04:36.564 --> 04:38.772
And I don't care
who knows it!

04:38.772 --> 04:41.079
You know, Chris,
you've got a grandpa

04:41.079 --> 04:42.754
who could use
your help right now.

04:42.754 --> 04:45.433
I'm sure he'd enjoy
spending time with you.

04:45.433 --> 04:50.149
Okay... I'll give
it a shot.

04:50.149 --> 04:51.725
You're not gonna
kill yourself, are you?

04:51.725 --> 04:54.274
That would be a severe black
mark on my record as a mom.

04:54.274 --> 04:57.784
Oh, I'd have to make up stories
of a severe mental illness.

04:57.784 --> 05:00.495
Make is seem a miracle
you made it this long.

05:00.495 --> 05:06.694
I could do that.

05:06.694 --> 05:08.472
Sucks about your leg, Grandpa.

05:08.472 --> 05:09.906
How you been doin'?

05:09.906 --> 05:11.753
Well, let me tell you,
this is awful.

05:11.753 --> 05:13.057
I-I'm so bored.

05:13.057 --> 05:15.263
I can't sleep,
I-I just have to lie here

05:15.263 --> 05:17.140
and wait for my
stupid leg to heal.

05:17.140 --> 05:19.046
Oh, I'm really
sorry, Grandpa.

05:19.046 --> 05:21.325
And the worst part about it,
is I can't have sex.

05:21.325 --> 05:24.163
God! I wish there was a way
I could just do it myself.

05:24.163 --> 05:27.114
You know, just-just to be done
and napping within four minutes.

05:27.114 --> 05:30.366
Let me show you something.

05:30.366 --> 05:34.078
That... was... amazing!

05:34.078 --> 05:36.384
And Lynda Carter
wasn't actually here?

05:36.384 --> 05:38.402
No! That was just
in your mind.

05:38.402 --> 05:39.566
Incredible!

05:39.566 --> 05:40.710
So-So you can do that like,

05:40.710 --> 05:42.244
wh-what, once a year
or something?

05:42.244 --> 05:43.820
No. You can do it basically

05:43.820 --> 05:45.497
whenever you're not
doing something else.

05:45.497 --> 05:46.831
Cool!

05:46.831 --> 05:50.914
Hey, next time I want to
try it with my hand.

05:50.914 --> 05:53.694
Hey, Grandpa.
What should we do now?

05:53.694 --> 05:55.107
You wanna order a pizza?

05:55.107 --> 05:56.573
Well, that doesn't sound
very exciting.

05:56.573 --> 05:59.793
But now you can
follow your order online!

05:59.793 --> 06:00.997
(keyboard clicking)

06:00.997 --> 06:01.900
There it is.
It's on Van Buren!

06:01.900 --> 06:03.236
Oh. Oh. He's almost here!

06:03.236 --> 06:06.216
Wow, he's really fast.
Hey, I got an idea,

06:06.216 --> 06:08.563
let's put in two different
orders and have 'em race!

06:08.563 --> 06:10.802
(gasps) You think it'll
crash the system?

06:10.802 --> 06:13.861
Only one way to find out.
(keyboard clicking)

06:13.861 --> 06:15.899
Here's your pizza.
That's $16.50.

06:15.899 --> 06:17.533
We were playing
a game with you.

06:17.533 --> 06:19.380
That's what you are.
You're a clown.

06:19.380 --> 06:20.845
Are you gonna
pay for the pizza?

06:20.845 --> 06:23.323
Yes. Your money is in
this pile of mashed potatoes.

06:23.323 --> 06:26.102
Eat your way out. No hands.

06:26.102 --> 06:27.949
(munching, moaning)

06:27.949 --> 06:30.758
This is fun, Chris.
I like hanging out with you.

06:30.758 --> 06:32.635
Don't look up.
You're not a part of this.

06:32.635 --> 06:36.788
♪

06:36.788 --> 06:38.794
It's sounding really
good, Grandpa.

06:38.794 --> 06:40.271
I know, I know.

06:40.271 --> 06:41.304
Sorry I'm late.

06:41.304 --> 06:43.280
Look, Jason, are you
taking this seriously?

06:43.280 --> 06:45.056
Because Chris and I
take this seriously.

06:45.056 --> 06:47.293
You know, if you're not
gonna show up to rehearsal,

06:47.293 --> 06:49.140
we'll find someone else
who will, all right?

06:49.140 --> 06:51.788
We want to get some paying gigs!
Sorry. Geez.

06:51.788 --> 06:55.372
Remember, this is about writing music
that means something to us!

06:55.372 --> 06:58.311
Okay, from the top.

06:58.311 --> 07:00.258
♪ Halls Mentho-lyptus

07:00.258 --> 07:02.535
♪ You can feel it
in your nose ♪

07:02.535 --> 07:05.315
♪ That's how you know
it's a medicated cough drop ♪

07:05.315 --> 07:07.250
♪ And not just a candy.

07:07.250 --> 07:09.559
Hey, can we play
one of my songs?

07:09.559 --> 07:12.578
No! No one wants to hear
your stupid songs about nothing!

07:12.578 --> 07:16.692
Now, let's play "I Fell in the Shower,
So Maybe We Do Need That Bar."

07:16.692 --> 07:21.449
Five, six,
seven, eight!

07:21.449 --> 07:23.485
Listen, Chris, I really
want to thank you

07:23.485 --> 07:26.365
for coming to take care of me
and helping me get well again.

07:26.365 --> 07:28.642
Oh, it was no big deal.
Well, it is to me,

07:28.642 --> 07:31.121
and I want to give you some
money for all your time.

07:31.121 --> 07:32.827
Come on, y-you don't
have to do that.

07:32.827 --> 07:35.978
I just like getting to spend time
with my grandpa, you know?

07:35.978 --> 07:38.256
I... Wait, wait, what?

07:38.256 --> 07:40.262
You're... you're not
gonna take the money?

07:40.262 --> 07:42.169
No, I don't want
your money.

07:42.169 --> 07:44.115
I had fun
hanging out with you.

07:44.115 --> 07:46.022
Well, all right, then.

07:46.022 --> 07:47.828
Hey, Grandpa,
check it out.

07:47.828 --> 07:49.432
When I make
my elbow like this,

07:49.432 --> 07:51.750
it looks like
women's private parts!

07:51.750 --> 07:54.761
(laughs): Oh, Chris! You just
have a way of looking at things

07:54.761 --> 07:58.644
that's delightfully fresh!

07:58.644 --> 08:01.283
(both laughing)

08:01.283 --> 08:03.058
We're not supposed
to be doing this.

08:03.058 --> 08:06.580
I bet we're not supposed
to be doing this.

08:06.583 --> 08:08.617
Daddy!
You're all better!

08:08.617 --> 08:09.500
That's right, pumpkin.

08:09.500 --> 08:11.396
And I have an important
announcement to make.

08:11.396 --> 08:14.006
I have decided
to change my will,

08:14.006 --> 08:15.983
and name
my grandson Chris

08:15.983 --> 08:18.460
the sole heir
to the Pewterschmidt fortune.

08:18.460 --> 08:20.066
You what?
What? Oh, my!

08:20.066 --> 08:21.440
(clattering in distance)

08:21.440 --> 08:25.615
Oh, no!
My hairless twin got out!

08:25.622 --> 08:28.746
(gunshot)

08:28.748 --> 08:30.049
Hello, family.

08:30.049 --> 08:37.263
Let's eat all
the garbage we want.

08:37.263 --> 08:40.576
Daddy, you're seriously leaving
your entire estate to Chris?

08:40.576 --> 08:42.621
I-I mean,
what about Mom?

08:42.621 --> 08:45.391
I promise she'll be dead
before I am. I promise.

08:45.391 --> 08:47.538
But, Grandpa, I don't
even want the money.

08:47.538 --> 08:50.016
See? This is exactly
why you should get it!

08:50.016 --> 08:51.191
So refreshing!

08:51.191 --> 08:52.927
Well, I-I don't
want it, either.

08:52.927 --> 08:54.501
Good, 'cause
you're not getting it.

08:54.501 --> 08:56.006
Come on, what
are you doing?

08:56.006 --> 08:58.214
Listen, Carter, you take
me out of your will,

08:58.214 --> 09:00.291
I'm taking you
out of mine.

09:00.291 --> 09:03.271
Peter, that wasn't your will,
that was your birth certificate.

09:03.271 --> 09:04.374
Oh, no!

09:04.374 --> 09:05.589
(gasps)

09:05.589 --> 09:06.953
There's no light!

09:06.953 --> 09:08.800
There's only fire!

09:08.800 --> 09:11.539
Look, Carter, I suppose you're
entitled to do what you want,

09:11.539 --> 09:14.018
but, you know, I'm just
saying, if it were me,

09:14.018 --> 09:16.135
I would give all the
money to charity.

09:16.135 --> 09:17.338
Oh, yeah?
Which charity?

09:17.338 --> 09:18.804
Well, there are
just so many

09:18.804 --> 09:20.550
that do such
great work.

09:20.550 --> 09:21.784
Name just one.

09:21.784 --> 09:23.630
Um... well,
you know...

09:23.630 --> 09:26.308
Poor... Green...

09:26.308 --> 09:28.044
Whale... Guns...

09:28.044 --> 09:29.289
Books?

09:29.289 --> 09:31.397
You are
such a fraud.

09:31.397 --> 09:39.102
Why won't anyone help us?!

09:39.102 --> 09:41.168
What the hell?
I can't believe your dad's

09:41.168 --> 09:42.715
giving all his cash
to Chris!

09:42.715 --> 09:45.422
I know it's strange,
but in the end it's his money,

09:45.422 --> 09:47.028
so who really cares?

09:47.028 --> 09:48.604
Well, yeah, but...

09:48.604 --> 09:50.179
But what?

09:50.179 --> 09:53.230
Peter... did you marry
me for my money?

09:53.230 --> 09:55.637
Of course not, Lois,
but even you can't deny

09:55.637 --> 09:57.845
it was always gonna
be a huge perk.

09:57.845 --> 10:00.825
D-Did I use that right? Perk?
Yes, Peter.

10:00.825 --> 10:02.852
Yeah, I thought so,
but then it just sounded

10:02.852 --> 10:04.237
kind of weird when I said it.

10:04.237 --> 10:05.541
It was fine.
Thanks.

10:05.541 --> 10:08.461
Anyway, I don't plan on losing out
on any of that money.

10:08.461 --> 10:11.742
So if you ask me, we got to start
sucking up to Chris right away.

10:11.742 --> 10:13.678
What? Wh-What are
you talking about?

10:13.678 --> 10:15.554
I'm talking about
brownnosing Chris

10:15.554 --> 10:17.561
and getting on
his good side perk.

10:17.561 --> 10:19.376
No, that's wrong.
No "perk."

10:19.376 --> 10:22.346
Okay, my bad. But I've been
counting on that money, Lois.

10:22.346 --> 10:24.766
It's always been critical
to my master plan.

10:24.766 --> 10:26.240
What master plan?

10:26.240 --> 10:28.478
Look, I never
told you this, but...

10:28.478 --> 10:31.658
for years now, I've been
planning on retiring at 45

10:31.658 --> 10:36.334
so I can work on finding a cure for
Ballzheimers disease.

10:36.341 --> 10:37.890
Peter, are
those testicles?

10:37.890 --> 10:39.494
Wh-where did
you get those?

10:39.494 --> 10:45.486
(crying):
I don't remember!

10:45.486 --> 10:48.063
Hey, hey, there he is!

10:48.063 --> 10:50.974
Oh, boy, hot dogs and
Nintendo, huh, Chris?

10:50.974 --> 10:53.191
Dad, what are you doing?
What's going on?

10:53.191 --> 10:54.354
(laughs)

10:54.354 --> 10:55.529
Good one, Chris!

10:55.529 --> 10:56.532
(laughing)

10:56.532 --> 10:58.379
Good one!
Why are you dressed like that?

10:58.379 --> 11:00.085
I don't know. I-I
just kind of felt

11:00.085 --> 11:01.590
like this is what
cool people wear.

11:01.590 --> 11:04.138
Hey, hey, Chris, how about you
and me do a secret handshake

11:04.138 --> 11:06.245
that has way too many steps
to remember, all right?

11:06.245 --> 11:09.053
Okay. Shake, bump, bump,
slap, pinky hook,

11:09.053 --> 11:11.703
pretend to slick your hair back,
represent, bump,

11:11.703 --> 11:13.609
one spin, slap high, slap low,

11:13.609 --> 11:16.218
reverse spin, bump, explode,
shake, belly rub,

11:16.218 --> 11:18.697
fake yawn, finger gun,
hitchhiker, hitchhiker,

11:18.697 --> 11:21.005
shimmy shimmy sham sham,
shake, shake, shake, bump,

11:21.005 --> 11:22.611
something smells
and shake again.

11:22.611 --> 11:25.951
Okay, ready?

11:25.958 --> 11:30.446
Oh, my God, it's nighttime.

11:30.446 --> 11:33.868
MAN (on TV): We now return to the director's
cut of Mission: Impossible 5,

11:33.868 --> 11:36.446
with the step stools
not edited out.

11:36.446 --> 11:38.985
You're coming with me because
I'm definitely over six feet,

11:38.985 --> 11:40.490
and you're not handsome.

11:40.490 --> 11:42.235
Hey, Chris, hey,
you remember that kid

11:42.235 --> 11:43.912
you said was bullying
you at school?

11:43.912 --> 11:45.046
Well, here's his head!

11:45.046 --> 11:46.179
(screaming)

11:46.179 --> 11:47.555
That's not even him!

11:47.555 --> 11:49.099
That's the deaf kid!

11:49.099 --> 11:51.035
Oh, that was
sign language.

11:51.035 --> 11:53.052
I thought he was
trying to defend himself

11:53.052 --> 11:57.035
with terrible karate.

11:57.035 --> 12:01.019
Chris, I want to share with you
a timeworn father/son tradition.

12:01.019 --> 12:02.926
I am gonna show you
a film comedy

12:02.926 --> 12:05.164
from my youth
that won't hold up.

12:05.164 --> 12:07.711
Welcome to the classic comedy,
Meatballs.

12:07.711 --> 12:09.116
Oh, that sounds great.

12:09.116 --> 12:11.164
Is it about a pasta
factory or something?

12:11.164 --> 12:12.568
No, that's part of the joke.

12:12.568 --> 12:13.942
Who's the guy?

12:13.942 --> 12:15.910
That's not a guy.
That's the hot chick!

12:15.910 --> 12:17.255
Where are her boobs?

12:17.255 --> 12:19.160
Flat with a decent face
was the best

12:19.160 --> 12:20.364
we could hope for back then.

12:20.364 --> 12:22.612
Miley Cyrus had sex
with a foam finger

12:22.612 --> 12:24.750
at, like, 6:00 p.m.
Central Time.

12:24.750 --> 12:26.966
This movie has a canoe
that slowly sinks.

12:26.966 --> 12:28.832
All right, you know what?
Forget it!

12:28.832 --> 12:31.681
I'm just gonna take my VCR,
my VCR head-cleaning tape,

12:31.681 --> 12:34.592
my VCR head-cleaning spray,
my head-cleaning rag,

12:34.592 --> 12:41.726
and my rewinder, and just
get the hell out of here.

12:41.726 --> 12:44.004
MAN (on TV):
We now return to At the Movies

12:44.004 --> 12:46.712
With Two Guys Who Watch
the Films On Their iPhones.

12:46.712 --> 12:48.188
Good evening.
First off, we're going

12:48.188 --> 12:49.935
to review Paul Greengrass'
Captain Phillips.

12:49.935 --> 12:51.539
What did you think, Bill?

12:51.539 --> 12:53.044
Well, it got off
to a great start,

12:53.044 --> 12:55.452
but when it was my turn
to play Words With Friends,

12:55.452 --> 12:56.796
it really took
me out of it.

12:56.796 --> 12:58.402
Well, that's a shame,
because visually...

12:58.402 --> 13:00.540
(phone whooshes)
Ooh!

13:00.540 --> 13:04.422
ANNOUNCER: When we come back, the guys
will review American Hustle.

13:04.422 --> 13:05.897
Hmm?

13:05.897 --> 13:07.604
Hey, you guys.

13:07.604 --> 13:09.078
Geez, Peter,
you look exhausted.

13:09.078 --> 13:11.286
Ugh, I am. I've
been busting my ass

13:11.286 --> 13:13.633
for the last week trying
to suck up to Chris.

13:13.633 --> 13:15.310
To Chris?
What the hell for?

13:15.310 --> 13:16.573
Well, Carter
kind of decided

13:16.573 --> 13:18.449
he's gonna leave all
his money to Chris.

13:18.449 --> 13:20.627
So, I've been trying to
get on his good side.

13:20.627 --> 13:22.574
I even cleaned his room
for him the other day.

13:22.574 --> 13:25.273
Wish I hadn't done that.

13:25.279 --> 13:27.731
Chris, our
bath is ready.

13:27.731 --> 13:29.567
I... uh...

13:29.567 --> 13:31.674
I don't... I don't know
what to do now.

13:31.674 --> 13:33.922
I... I don't have
the parenting skills necessary

13:33.922 --> 13:35.126
to deal with this.

13:35.126 --> 13:37.073
I say we never
speak of this again.

13:37.073 --> 13:39.310
I... I might move.

13:39.310 --> 13:41.357
You know what?
I say, good for Chris

13:41.357 --> 13:43.764
and whatever lucky girl
he ends up marrying.

13:43.764 --> 13:46.202
Yeah, or lucky guy,
if he ends up being gay.

13:46.202 --> 13:47.778
Lucky guy?

13:47.778 --> 13:49.353
Wait a minute.

13:49.353 --> 13:51.500
You guys just gave me an idea!

13:51.500 --> 13:52.866
(playing tuba)

13:52.866 --> 13:54.039
(laughs)

13:54.039 --> 13:56.488
What's he doing up there?
He's a cat!

13:56.488 --> 13:59.498
He can't play no tuba!

13:59.498 --> 14:00.873
No, wait!

14:00.873 --> 14:03.150
Actually, you guys
gave me two ideas!

14:03.150 --> 14:04.554
(snoring)

14:04.554 --> 14:08.668
Mumbling while I sleep
to indicate dream content.

14:08.668 --> 14:10.145
Chris, Chris, wake up.

14:10.145 --> 14:12.291
I have something very
important to ask you.

14:12.291 --> 14:15.531
Chris, there comes a time when
every man looks at his son

14:15.531 --> 14:21.662
and thinks, "I want to take
this to the next level."

14:21.662 --> 14:25.214
Chris Griffin...
will you marry me?

14:25.214 --> 14:28.596
What?! Is it even legal
for a man to marry his son?

14:28.596 --> 14:30.030
It is in Vermont.

14:30.030 --> 14:32.137
As long as it's a man and a
man, anything goes up there.

14:32.137 --> 14:34.054
They're a bunch of
liberal degenerates.

14:34.054 --> 14:35.991
I don't know.
It seems really weird.

14:35.991 --> 14:38.239
I mean, aren't men
supposed to marry women?

14:38.239 --> 14:40.916
No, no, no, that's just
all of human history

14:40.916 --> 14:42.554
except for the
last five months.

14:42.554 --> 14:44.158
We'll just be
like best pals.

14:44.158 --> 14:45.763
And besides, there's
plenty of people

14:45.763 --> 14:47.480
who are married
and don't have sex.

14:47.480 --> 14:49.085
Like Will Smith
and that pit bull.

14:49.085 --> 14:51.022
Why do you even
want to marry me?

14:51.022 --> 14:53.398
It's time to settle down
and simplify things,

14:53.398 --> 14:56.209
like maybe having one ATM
card and one bank account.

14:56.209 --> 14:57.684
Say, yours.

14:57.684 --> 15:00.704
Oh. I get it.

15:00.704 --> 15:03.544
So, what do you say?

15:03.548 --> 15:06.492
When you're married, you get
to spend all your time together,

15:06.492 --> 15:09.373
doing things like playing catch
and going fishing, right?

15:09.373 --> 15:11.410
Well, the best marriages
give each other space,

15:11.410 --> 15:12.654
but, yes, Chris.

15:12.654 --> 15:15.333
Then, yes, I will
marry you, Dad!

15:15.333 --> 15:17.812
Oh, that's
wonderful news!

15:17.812 --> 15:20.180
You should know this
ring is very special.

15:20.180 --> 15:22.157
It used to belong
to your mother.

15:22.157 --> 15:24.173
Wait. What about Mom?

15:24.173 --> 15:26.039
I'm afraid that's
over, Chris.

15:26.039 --> 15:27.253
Lois, wake up.

15:27.253 --> 15:29.360
I need you to sign
this legal document.

15:29.360 --> 15:31.267
Huh? Wha-What is this?

15:31.267 --> 15:33.405
It's a petition
to force that hot mom

15:33.405 --> 15:35.581
to wear something appropriate
at PTA meetings.

15:35.581 --> 15:40.909
Oh, thank God.

15:40.909 --> 15:42.915
(cans rattling, tires squeaking)

15:42.915 --> 15:48.203
(engine revving)

15:48.203 --> 15:49.909
No, Dad.

15:49.909 --> 15:58.348
I don't know
what normal is anymore.

16:01.168 --> 16:03.946
So now you know my complete
sexual history, Chris.

16:03.946 --> 16:07.498
Wow. I'm surprised you got
fooled by a bear in a wig.

16:07.498 --> 16:09.767
It wasn't a wig,
it was a hair system.

16:09.767 --> 16:11.211
Well, whatever.

16:11.211 --> 16:13.088
Why do we have
all these appointments?

16:13.088 --> 16:15.064
Wedding DJ, florist.

16:15.064 --> 16:17.874
Because, Chris, it takes time
to plan a perfect wedding.

16:17.874 --> 16:19.549
You don't want
to jump the gun.

16:19.549 --> 16:22.028
You know, like when you
respond to a text too quickly.

16:22.028 --> 16:35.709
(whooshing)

16:35.709 --> 16:37.960
So, should we get started
with your bridal registry?

16:37.960 --> 16:39.939
Yeah, um, I'd like
to furnish my kitchen

16:39.939 --> 16:42.145
as if I'm the greatest
chef in the world,

16:42.145 --> 16:43.420
even though I've
never cooked before.

16:43.420 --> 16:45.025
That's what we do!
Okay, great.

16:45.025 --> 16:46.932
All right, we'll start
with the nine grand

16:46.932 --> 16:53.764
in copper-bottom
cookware.

16:53.764 --> 16:56.102
Holy wack-a-zoly!

16:56.102 --> 16:57.447
Dad!
What?

16:57.447 --> 16:59.785
Don't "what" me.
You know what you did.

16:59.785 --> 17:06.286
Hey, I may be your husband and
your dad, but I'm still a man.

17:06.286 --> 17:08.694
Yeah, we're looking to plan our
post-wedding Sunday breakfast.

17:08.694 --> 17:10.471
You know,
when everyone's sick of us.

17:10.471 --> 17:11.673
Of course.

17:11.673 --> 17:13.782
Excellent. Do you have
a table for the couple

17:13.782 --> 17:16.130
that barely made it through
the weekend without breaking up?

17:16.130 --> 17:17.905
Absolutely. Can I put
them near the couple

17:17.905 --> 17:20.072
that hooked up drunk and now
have to make awkward small talk

17:20.072 --> 17:21.618
until their cab to
the airport arrives?

17:21.618 --> 17:23.093
Sure. And maybe
they could go next

17:23.093 --> 17:24.599
to the vastly-underdressed
cousin

17:24.599 --> 17:26.404
who thinks
the world revolves around him?

17:26.404 --> 17:27.949
I have just the spot.

17:27.949 --> 17:29.283
Will there be a
physically-frail,

17:29.283 --> 17:30.458
fall-down uncle?

17:30.458 --> 17:32.334
Indeed. And we'd like
to have him walk

17:32.334 --> 17:33.699
through a maze
of chair legs.

17:33.699 --> 17:35.043
Anything else?
Yes.

17:35.043 --> 17:36.477
We did invite
a black couple.

17:36.477 --> 17:38.825
Um, even though we only met them
three months ago,

17:38.825 --> 17:40.872
but we would like them
to be prominently featured

17:40.872 --> 17:47.765
to let the other guests know how
tolerant and wonderful we are.

17:47.765 --> 17:49.742
I'm excited for
your first dance.

17:49.742 --> 17:51.448
And now we're
ready to add music.

17:51.448 --> 17:52.652
What's your song?

17:52.652 --> 17:54.560
You know, I've given it
a lot of thought,

17:54.560 --> 17:56.735
and I went with the most
romantic song ever,

17:56.735 --> 18:00.247
"Stars And Stripes Forever"
by John Philip Sousa.

18:00.247 --> 18:01.361
♪

18:01.361 --> 18:02.626
March! March!
March! March!

18:02.626 --> 18:04.402
Can you feel the
soldiers, Chris?

18:04.402 --> 18:05.776
So many have fallen.

18:05.776 --> 18:07.453
And this is why
they were fighting.

18:07.453 --> 18:09.289
For a man to marry his son

18:09.289 --> 18:10.794
in a state with
enough trees around

18:10.794 --> 18:14.114
that nobody can
see what's going on.

18:14.114 --> 18:19.001
(organ plays gentle melody)

18:19.001 --> 18:21.207
It was nice of the
guests at the cat funeral

18:21.207 --> 18:22.583
to stay for our wedding.

18:22.583 --> 18:24.319
Yeah, and I bet
you're especially happy

18:24.319 --> 18:25.963
we're getting married
on a Thursday.

18:25.963 --> 18:27.740
School, yuck, right?!

18:27.740 --> 18:30.018
Welcome, friends, loved ones,

18:30.018 --> 18:32.697
and people who are waiting
for the 3:00 check-in time

18:32.697 --> 18:33.861
with nothing better to do.

18:33.861 --> 18:35.677
Just let us put
our bags in there.

18:35.677 --> 18:38.054
I'm literally gonna
grab my shorts and leave.

18:38.054 --> 18:42.099
I understand the two of you
have written your own vows?

18:42.099 --> 18:43.905
Chris, to express my love,

18:43.905 --> 18:46.985
I turn to the words of the only
poet that blue collar,

18:46.985 --> 18:50.638
New England scumbags
like me know: Robert Frost.

18:50.638 --> 18:53.587
"Two roads diverged
in a wood, and I...

18:53.587 --> 18:56.226
I took the one less traveled."

18:56.226 --> 18:58.673
Now, I ain't no scholar,
but if that's not a metaphor

18:58.673 --> 19:01.083
for major-league butt stuff,
I don't know what is.

19:01.083 --> 19:02.758
Thank you. Chris?

19:02.758 --> 19:05.838
LOIS:
Stop the wedding!

19:05.838 --> 19:08.146
Lois! How did you
find out about this?

19:08.146 --> 19:09.853
Peter, several people
have called the police

19:09.853 --> 19:11.367
about a man marrying his son.

19:11.367 --> 19:12.803
It's not normal!

19:12.803 --> 19:15.311
Peter? Peter
Griffin?

19:15.311 --> 19:17.257
Oh, God.

19:17.257 --> 19:18.892
Is everyone
from your past here

19:18.892 --> 19:20.698
to walk you down
the aisle?!

19:20.698 --> 19:22.174
Peter, you
cannot do this!

19:22.174 --> 19:24.080
You cannot
marry your son!

19:24.080 --> 19:26.057
I don't care how much
money Daddy's left him.

19:26.057 --> 19:27.662
Don't listen
to your mother, Chris.

19:27.662 --> 19:29.339
It's 'cause of her
we have bedtimes!

19:29.339 --> 19:31.314
Chris, come on,
we're going home!

19:31.314 --> 19:33.019
He can't make
you do this.

19:33.019 --> 19:35.097
But, Mom,
I want to do this.

19:35.097 --> 19:36.441
What?

19:36.441 --> 19:40.154
I know he's marrying me
for my money, but I don't care.

19:40.154 --> 19:42.934
Dad and I spent more time
together planning this wedding

19:42.934 --> 19:44.569
than we ever have before.

19:44.569 --> 19:46.114
And if being married means

19:46.114 --> 19:50.229
I get to spend even more time
with my dad, then it's worth it.

19:50.229 --> 19:54.614
Wait. You knew all along I
just wanted you for your money?

19:54.614 --> 19:57.060
Yeah, Dad, I did.

19:57.060 --> 19:59.208
Wow.

19:59.208 --> 20:01.788
Oh, boy, I've
been a real jerk.

20:01.788 --> 20:03.292
I'm sorry, Chris.

20:03.292 --> 20:04.898
But you know what?

20:04.898 --> 20:07.276
I'm gonna make it up to
you, starting right now.

20:07.276 --> 20:10.686
Chris Griffin...
will you be my son?

20:10.686 --> 20:12.894
Yes, Dad.

20:12.894 --> 20:17.249
OMG, the photographer is,
like, obsessed with me.

20:17.249 --> 20:19.828
Well, let's all go home,
you guys.

20:19.828 --> 20:22.075
I think we've had enough
excitement for one day.

20:22.075 --> 20:24.041
Yeah, and
I guess I learned

20:24.041 --> 20:25.858
it's wrong to take
your son to Vermont

20:25.858 --> 20:27.263
under false
pretenses

20:27.263 --> 20:29.240
to try to marry him
for his inheritance.

20:29.240 --> 20:30.373
You... you should've
known that.

20:30.373 --> 20:32.279
Well, we should
probably get going.

20:32.279 --> 20:34.838
I think this
adventure is over.

20:34.838 --> 20:37.698
PETER: Interestingly, however,
I did run into Chris again.

20:37.698 --> 20:40.005
It was on the Upper West
Side of Manhattan.

20:40.005 --> 20:42.715
He was with another dad.
I was with another son.

20:42.715 --> 20:45.173
But it was nice reminiscing
about old times.

20:45.173 --> 20:46.346
For you kids watching,

20:46.346 --> 20:48.294
this is a reference
to a Woody Allen movie.

20:48.294 --> 20:50.300
He also married one
of his children.

20:50.301 --> 21:51.301
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru